{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfjQkbstKVFiTn8E44SUZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rewritten the repair candidate and it passes the admission self-check. I couldn't check novelty here, so whether it clears that gate is still open.\n\n**What changed:** the first attempt added an additive left-first anchoring term, which predicted almost exactly like `second_order_motif_side_habit` (RMSE 0.00122, under the 0.002 threshold). The new mechanism, `pair_randomness_contrast_gain`, has the pair act as a shared reference point. A fixed, parameter-free measure of how random the pair looks overall scales how sharply the difference between the two sequences is felt. It multiplies that difference by exp(`lam` · z), where z is the pair's standardised mean per-flip randomness under a fair coin versus regular generators, and the sign of `lam` is fitted. Everything else is kept from the incumbent: each person's own believed switch rate and second-order switch belief, the three regular generators with each person's motif suspicion, the per-flip length weighting, and each person's side habit.\n\n**Test fit** (2 chains × 300 draws, my own script):\n- **The effect is real:** `lam` = −0.11 ± 0.03 (94% interval −0.17 to −0.06). People are more decisive between two regular-looking sequences and closer to a toss-up between two random-looking ones. Across this experiment's pairs, that scales the evidence by about 0.95× to 1.57×. Because the effect is clearly away from zero, the model should predict differently from the incumbent, but the novelty gate is the real test.\n- **Fit:** ELPD-LOO −2097.2 ± 37.7, against the incumbent's −2103.4. That is about 6 nats better.\n- **Sampling:** no divergences. The bulk ESS for `mu_w` was only 83 in this short run, and admission needs at least 100, so its longer 4-chain fit has to get there.\n\n`check_candidate` printed OK. Its smoke ELPD of −29226 comes from a 100-draw single-chain run that hadn't converged and doesn't reflect the model.\n\nAn earlier version computed the pair's level from the model's own parameters. It diverged on every draw, and computing the level from fixed inputs fixed that.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_1_repair_1/`:\n- hypothesis.md\n- model_name.txt\n- candidate.py"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1912,"cache_read_input_tokens":85171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1912,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8800eb0d-5c65-4eba-bbd0-e11e8d09a2bc","uuid":"e540b7b8-ff42-4ccd-99fc-835d039c39f3","timestamp":"2026-10-05T16:32:00.615Z","request_id":"req_011CfjQkbTqBUHif7j9NZPkv"}
